# Drafted by Gemini (R11c oak), edited.

~ start
Narrator: Dark sap weeps from the old oak as a dozen wooden eyelids creak open. Iron and wet earth rise from the roots as carved mouths move together.
quest souls_of_the_oak whispers
* Listen to the faces -> listen
* Ask who they are -> names
* [if level >= 6] Stand ground -> fight
* [if level < 6] Hold still and wait it out -> quiet
* Back away -> quiet

~ listen
Narrator: A dry chorus rustles like dead leaves on stone: their roots are parched, they are tired of the dark, and the axe took them for crimes they never did.
Narrator: Wooden teeth click together in a ragged plea: cut the boughs, split the heartwood, and let us out.
-> start

~ names
Narrator: Three faces near the base strain forward in splintered breaths. A gaunt woman claims she only took barley bread; a man swears the boundary stone was moved before he plowed.
Narrator: Highest of the three, the broad, scarred likeness of Gory Gus groans through a split lip, begging you to hack him free of the sap before the tree drinks the last of his name.
-> start

~ fight
Narrator: The great boughs groan like a gallows under weight, and the roots wrench themselves from the soil of the Round in a shower of cold dirt and sour blood.
quest souls_of_the_oak woken
set wm_oak_woken
combat wm_oak_wakes

~ quiet
Narrator: You step back onto the cobblestones, and one by one the wooden eyelids pinch shut until only blind bark remains under the leering moon.
-> END

~ freed
quest souls_of_the_oak freed
set wm_oak_freed
Narrator: A long, warm sigh passes through the shattered trunk as the carved mouths slacken, smoothing back into plain timber one by one until the bark is blind and still.
-> END
